  <name>Slidewire</name>
  <summary>Control app and device volumes with a MIDI controller</summary>
  <developer id="dev.briggen">
    <name>Nils Briggen</name>
  </developer>
  <description>
    <p>
      Slidewire turns a MIDI controller such as the Korg nanoKONTROL2 into a volume mixer for your desktop.
      Faders set the volume of apps and audio devices, buttons mute and switch them, and the LEDs show what's happening.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Faders for the focused app, specific apps, "all other apps", or any device</li>
      <li>Banks and scenes, soft takeover, per-strip range, curve, name and colour</li>
      <li>Buses that mix apps together, ducking, and remembered output per app</li>
      <li>Buttons for media keys, OBS Studio, EasyEffects, push-to-talk and more</li>
      <li>Imports MIDI Mixer for Windows profiles, so its presets for many controllers work</li>
      <li>Works with PipeWire and PulseAudio, on KDE Plasma, Hyprland, sway and other desktops</li>
    </ul>
  </description>
